WEBVTT

00:00:13.948 --> 00:00:15.508
Okay, grab shell, dude.

00:00:15.588 --> 00:00:17.748
Grab what?

00:00:27.508 --> 00:00:29.268
Righteous! Righteous!

00:00:34.268 --> 00:00:35.788
So,

00:00:36.628 --> 00:00:40.348
what brings you on this fine day
to the EAC?

00:00:40.428 --> 00:00:43.428
Well, Dory and I need to get to Sydney.

00:00:43.508 --> 00:00:45.748
Dory! Is she all right?

00:00:46.148 --> 00:00:48.388
Oh, little blue.

00:00:48.468 --> 00:00:49.628
She is sub-level, dude.

00:00:53.828 --> 00:00:55.788
Dory, Dory! Dory!

00:00:56.788 --> 00:00:57.948
Oh, Dory.

00:00:58.228 --> 00:00:59.668
(DORY MUMBLES INCOHERENTLY)

00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:02.548
I'm so sorry.

00:01:03.228 --> 00:01:06.108
This is all my fault. It's my fault.

00:01:06.188 --> 00:01:09.188
...twenty-nine, 30!
Ready or not, here I come!

00:01:11.908 --> 00:01:13.028
There you are.

00:01:13.788 --> 00:01:15.228
Catch me if you can.

00:01:25.268 --> 00:01:27.028
Up you go!

00:01:29.068 --> 00:01:30.788
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:37.548 --> 00:01:38.828
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:38.908 --> 00:01:43.028
Kill the motor, dude.
Let us see what Squirt does flying solo.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.668
Whoa! That was so cool.

00:01:54.748 --> 00:01:57.508
Hey, Dad. Did you see that?
Did you see me?

00:01:57.628 --> 00:02:01.788
-Did you see what I did?
-You so totally rock, Squirt.

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.588
Give me some fin.

00:02:03.668 --> 00:02:04.708
Noggin.

00:02:04.788 --> 00:02:06.108
Dude.

00:02:06.948 --> 00:02:11.628
Intro. Jellyman, Offspring.
Offspring, Jellyman.

00:02:11.708 --> 00:02:15.148
-Jellies? Sweet.
-Totally.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:18.468
I must have done
something you all liked, dudes.

00:02:18.548 --> 00:02:20.708
-You rock, dude.
-Ow.

00:02:21.588 --> 00:02:23.748
Curl away, my son.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.708
It's awesome, Jellyman.

00:02:25.788 --> 00:02:29.228
When the little dudes are eggs
we leave them on a beach to hatch,

00:02:29.468 --> 00:02:33.228
and coo-coo-cachoo, they find
their way back to the big ol' blue.

00:02:33.308 --> 00:02:35.428
-All by themselves?
-Yeah!

00:02:35.508 --> 00:02:38.388
But, dude, how do you know
when they're ready?

00:02:38.468 --> 00:02:42.708
You never really know, but when
they know, you'll know. You know?

00:02:45.948 --> 00:02:47.468
(LAUGHTER)

00:02:47.588 --> 00:02:50.108
-Hey, look, everybody.
-I know that dude.

00:02:50.188 --> 00:02:51.468
It's the Jellyman.

00:02:52.188 --> 00:02:54.988
-Well go on. Jump on him.
-Turtle pile!

00:02:55.068 --> 00:02:56.748
Wait. Kids!

00:02:56.828 --> 00:02:58.708
-You funny?
-Where's your shell?

00:02:58.788 --> 00:03:01.068
-Do your stripes come off?
-I need to breathe.

00:03:01.188 --> 00:03:03.388
Did you cross the jellyfish forest?

00:03:03.468 --> 00:03:06.508
-One at a time.
-Mr. Fish, did you die?

00:03:06.588 --> 00:03:08.668
Sorry. I was vague on the details.

00:03:08.748 --> 00:03:12.268
-So where are you going?
-You see, my son was taken.

00:03:12.348 --> 00:03:14.588
My son was taken away from me.

00:03:15.468 --> 00:03:17.388
-No way!
-What happened?

00:03:17.468 --> 00:03:20.428
No, kids. I don't want to talk about it.

00:03:20.588 --> 00:03:23.028
-Come on.
-Please.

00:03:24.628 --> 00:03:26.188
Well, okay.

00:03:26.268 --> 00:03:29.788
I live on this reef, a long way from here.

00:03:29.988 --> 00:03:32.068
This is going to be good. I can tell.

00:03:32.148 --> 00:03:36.308
My son, Nemo, he was mad at me.

00:03:37.028 --> 00:03:39.708
Maybe he wouldn't have done it
if I hadn't been so tough on him.

00:03:39.788 --> 00:03:41.188
I don't know.

00:03:41.268 --> 00:03:43.668
He swam in the open water to this boat

00:03:43.748 --> 00:03:47.228
and these divers appeared
and I tried to stop them.

00:03:47.308 --> 00:03:50.188
The boat was too fast,
so we swam out in the ocean...

00:03:50.268 --> 00:03:51.388
He couldn't stop them.

00:03:51.468 --> 00:03:54.268
Then Nemo's dad,
he swims out to the ocean

00:03:54.348 --> 00:03:56.588
and they bump into three sharks.

00:03:56.668 --> 00:03:59.108
He scares them away
by blowing them up.

00:03:59.188 --> 00:04:01.908
-That's amazing.
-Then dives thousands of feet...

00:04:01.988 --> 00:04:06.188
Straight into the dark. It's wicked
dark there. You can't see a thing.

00:04:06.268 --> 00:04:08.748
The only thing
they can see down there is...

00:04:08.828 --> 00:04:12.548
This big, horrible creature with
razor-sharp teeth! Nice parry.

00:04:12.628 --> 00:04:14.068
Then he has to blast his way...

00:04:14.148 --> 00:04:17.108
These fish have been
searching the ocean for days

00:04:17.228 --> 00:04:19.028
on the East Australian Current.

00:04:19.108 --> 00:04:21.148
He may be on his way here right now.

00:04:21.228 --> 00:04:22.868
That should put him in
Sydney Harbour...

00:04:22.948 --> 00:04:24.308
In a few days.

00:04:24.388 --> 00:04:26.348
This guy will stop at nothing...

00:04:26.428 --> 00:04:29.268
...stop at nothing until he finds his son.
I hope he makes it.

00:04:29.348 --> 00:04:32.188
That's one dedicated father,
if you ask me.

00:04:38.788 --> 00:04:41.268
Mine. Mine. Mine.

00:04:47.388 --> 00:04:50.108
Would you just shut up?

00:04:50.188 --> 00:04:53.988
-You're rats with wings.
-This bloke's looking for his boy, Nemo.

00:04:54.068 --> 00:04:57.748
-He was taken off the reef by divers...
-There. Take it.

00:04:58.788 --> 00:05:01.428
Say that again.
You said something about Nemo.

00:05:01.508 --> 00:05:03.228
Mine. Mine. Mine.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.228
(GROWLS)

00:05:05.948 --> 00:05:06.948
Mine.

00:05:07.068 --> 00:05:10.268
Last I heard,
he's heading towards the harbor.

00:05:10.348 --> 00:05:11.668
Brilliant!

00:05:25.428 --> 00:05:26.828
Is he doing okay?

00:05:26.908 --> 00:05:30.148
I don't know, but whatever you do,
don't mention D-A-R...

00:05:30.228 --> 00:05:33.268
It's okay.
I know who you're talking about.

00:05:41.588 --> 00:05:42.828
Gill?

00:05:45.268 --> 00:05:46.308
Gill?

00:05:47.788 --> 00:05:48.988
Hey, Sharkbait.

00:05:50.108 --> 00:05:53.468
-I'm sorry I couldn't stop...
-GILL: I'm the one who should be sorry.

00:05:54.748 --> 00:05:58.988
I was so ready to get out,
so ready to taste that ocean,

00:05:59.588 --> 00:06:02.348
I was willing to put you
in harm's way to get there.

00:06:03.628 --> 00:06:05.868
Nothing should be worth that.

00:06:07.348 --> 00:06:09.748
I'm sorry I couldn't get you
back to your father, kid.

00:06:13.988 --> 00:06:15.988
All right. Hey, hey, hey!

00:06:16.788 --> 00:06:18.188
-What the...
-Aaggh!

00:06:18.268 --> 00:06:21.908
Well, that's one way
to pull a tooth. (LAUGHS)

00:06:23.388 --> 00:06:27.388
Darn kids. Well, good thing
I pulled the right one, eh?

00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:28.708
Pssst!

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:30.908
Nigel, you just missed an extraction.

00:06:30.988 --> 00:06:33.708
Has he loosened
the periodontal ligament yet?

00:06:33.788 --> 00:06:36.028
What am I talking about?
Where's Nemo?

00:06:36.108 --> 00:06:37.708
I've got to speak with him.

00:06:37.788 --> 00:06:40.868
Your dad's been fighting the ocean
looking for you.

00:06:40.948 --> 00:06:42.908
My father? Really?

00:06:42.988 --> 00:06:44.868
He's traveled hundreds of miles.

00:06:44.948 --> 00:06:48.108
-He's been battling sharks and jellyfish.
-Sharks?

00:06:48.188 --> 00:06:51.108
-That can't be him.
-Are you sure? What was his name?

00:06:51.188 --> 00:06:53.228
Some sort of sport fish. Tuna? Trout?

00:06:53.308 --> 00:06:54.908
-Marlin?
-That's it.

00:06:54.988 --> 00:06:58.588
-The clownfish from the reef.
-It's my dad! He took on a shark!

00:06:58.668 --> 00:07:01.628
-I heard he took on three.
-Three?

00:07:01.708 --> 00:07:04.028
-Three sharks?
-That's 4,800 teeth!

00:07:04.108 --> 00:07:06.268
After you were taken by Diver Dan,

00:07:06.348 --> 00:07:08.388
your dad followed the boat
like a maniac.

00:07:08.468 --> 00:07:09.588
Really?

00:07:09.668 --> 00:07:13.268
He's giving it all he's got
and then three sharks capture him.

00:07:13.348 --> 00:07:16.148
He blows 'em up
and then dives thousands of feet

00:07:16.228 --> 00:07:18.708
and gets chased
by a monster with huge teeth!

00:07:18.788 --> 00:07:21.308
He ties this demon to a rock.
And his reward?

00:07:21.388 --> 00:07:23.788
He gets to battle a jellyfish forest.

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:26.988
Now he's with sea turtles
on the East Australian Current

00:07:27.068 --> 00:07:30.508
and the word is he's headed this way,
right now, to Sydney!

00:07:31.028 --> 00:07:34.628
-What a good daddy.
-He was looking for you after all.

00:07:38.428 --> 00:07:41.188
-He's swimming in the filter!
-Not again!

00:07:43.508 --> 00:07:44.508
Sharkbait!

00:07:46.548 --> 00:07:48.788
-No!
-You've got your life ahead of you.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.788
-We'll help you.
-Get him out.

